  "title": "SequenceCancelledError",
  "description": "Thrown into a sequence step that waits on something that was cancelled: a SequenceHandle cancelled elsewhere, or a SequenceOperation that settled as `cancelled`. Left uncaught, it ends the waiting step as `cancelled` rather than `failed`. It is also the abort reason of SequenceContext.signal.",
